#!/usr/bin/env bash
# bin/dev-nightly-refine — the nightly refinement loop is DISABLED.
#
# 83 unattended runs, each told to extend and self-score its own guide, grew the guides
# from ~1k to 40-52k lines with contradictory version claims. The guides were restored
# and scripts/check-guide-size.sh now fails CI above 3,000 lines. Refine runs are manual.
# This script registers nothing; any argument (including the old --register) is ignored.
set -euo pipefail

cat <<'EOF'
qa-agentic-team — nightly refinement loop is DISABLED.

Why: unattended, self-scored runs grew the reference guides to 40-52k lines with
contradictory version claims. Guides are now refined by hand, one at a time, and CI
(scripts/check-guide-size.sh) rejects any guide over 3,000 lines.

Run a single manual refine in Claude Code, then review the diff before committing:
  /qa-refine playwright            (or k6, cypress, detox, appium, ...)
  /lang-refine python              (or typescript, java, csharp, general, ...)
  /qa-methodology-refine flakiness (or tdd, bdd, coverage, ...)
  git diff -- '*/references/*'
EOF
